<title>USA: PG&amp;E Calif. nuke seen at full power Monday.</title>
<headline>PG&amp;E Calif. nuke seen at full power Monday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pacific Gas and Electric Co's 1,087 megawatt Diablo Canyon nuclear power unit 1 will likely return to full output Monday afternoon after reducing power for condenser cleaning, a company spokesman said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We estimate it will be back at full power by mid-afternoon today,&quot; spokesman Jeff Lewis said.</p>
<p>The Avila Beach, Calif unit was reduced to about 50 percent of capacity over the weekend for the cleaning.</p>
<p>Diablo Canyon unit 2, with a capacity of 1,073 megawatts, continued to operate at full output, Lewis said.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
